  "result": "Perfect! All 171 tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n**src/dates.js** \u2014 Added due date calculation:\n\n**`calculateDueDate(issueDate, terms)`** \u2014 Calculates due date based on payment terms:\n- `'NET14'` \u2192 14 days after issue date\n- `'NET30'` \u2192 30 days after issue date\n- `'EOM'` \u2192 Last day of the issue date's month\n- Returns `null` for invalid terms\n\n**src/errors.js** \u2014 Added error code:\n- `TERMS_INVALID`: Payment terms must be NET14, NET30, or EOM\n\n**src/invoices.js** \u2014 Updated `createInvoice`:\n- Now accepts optional `terms` parameter (defaults to `'NET30'`)\n- Validates terms using `calculateDueDate`\n- Sets `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` on the returned invoice\n- Returns `TERMS_INVALID` error for unknown terms\n\n**Tests** \u2014 17 new tests covering:\n- `calculateDueDate` for all term types (NET14, NET30, EOM)\n- EOM edge cases:\n  - First day of month \u2192 last day of month\n  - Last day of month \u2192 same day\n  - Short months (February)\n  - Leap years (Feb 29)\n  - December (31st)\n- Invalid terms return `null`\n- `createInvoice` default terms (NET30)\n- `createInvoice` with explicit terms (NET14, NET30, EOM)\n- TERMS_INVALID error for unknown terms\n\nAll 171 tests pass \u2713",
